title: 'pallet-transaction-payment: refundable surcharge on operational transactions to prevent spam'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Adds a refundable anti-spam surcharge on `Operational` transactions, controlled by the new
    `Config::OperationalFeeSurcharge` constant. When set to `N`, an extra `N * inclusion_fee`
    (tip excluded) is withdrawn upfront and refunded only if the dispatch succeeds, so failing
    operational transactions forfeit it while honest ones pay as before. Priority is unaffected.
    The surcharge is applied by `pallet-asset-tx-payment` and
    `pallet-asset-conversion-tx-payment` as well, for payments in the native currency and in an
    asset alike.

    Some dispatchables report success regardless of the outcome of the calls they dispatch, for
    example `Utility::batch`, `Utility::force_batch`, `Utility::if_else`, `Proxy::proxy`,
    `MetaTx::dispatch`, `Recovery::control_inherited_account` and the proposal execution in
    `pallet-collective`, and they can be `Operational` while reporting success. Those now note
    the failure of an inner dispatch in the new transient
    `frame_system::ExtrinsicNestedDispatchFailure` storage value, through
    `frame_system::Pallet::note_nested_dispatch_failure`, so that wrapping a failing operational
    call cannot recover the surcharge.

    Breaking: every runtime must now set `type OperationalFeeSurcharge`. Use `()` (the default,
    behavior unchanged) to keep it disabled; all in-tree runtimes do so.

